=================================================
          LINUX SPECIAL PERMISSIONS
=================================================

TYPES
-----

1. SUID       → 4
2. SGID       → 2
3. Sticky Bit → 1


=================================================
SUID (SET USER ID)
=================================================

Numeric Value → 4

Used Mainly   → Executable files

Purpose:
When executed, the program runs with
the effective permissions of the file owner.

SET:
chmod 4755 filename
chmod u+s filename

REMOVE:
chmod u-s filename

DISPLAY:
rwsr-xr-x → Execute + SUID
rwSr-xr-x → SUID without Execute


=================================================
SGID (SET GROUP ID)
=================================================

Numeric Value → 2

FILE:
Program runs with effective group
permissions of file group owner.

DIRECTORY:
New files/directories inherit the
group ownership of parent directory.

SET:
chmod 2755 filename
chmod g+s filename

REMOVE:
chmod g-s filename

DISPLAY:
rwxr-sr-x → Execute + SGID
rwxr-Sr-x → SGID without Execute


=================================================
STICKY BIT
=================================================

Numeric Value → 1

Used Mainly → Directories

Purpose:
Users cannot delete other users'
files in a shared directory.

SET:
chmod 1755 directory
chmod 1777 directory
chmod +t directory

REMOVE:
chmod -t directory

DISPLAY:
rwxrwxrwt → Execute + Sticky Bit
rwxrwxrwT → Sticky Bit without Execute

Example:
/tmp


=================================================
NUMERIC EXAMPLES
=================================================

4755 → SUID + rwxr-xr-x
2755 → SGID + rwxr-xr-x
1755 → Sticky + rwxr-xr-x

6755 → SUID + SGID + rwxr-xr-x
3755 → SGID + Sticky + rwxr-xr-x
7755 → SUID + SGID + Sticky + rwxr-xr-x


=================================================
SPECIAL PERMISSION POSITIONS
=================================================

rws rwx rwx
  ↑
SUID

rwx rws rwx
      ↑
     SGID

rwx rwx rwt
          ↑
      Sticky Bit


=================================================
SMALL vs CAPITAL
=================================================

s → Special permission + Execute
S → Special permission without Execute

t → Sticky Bit + Execute
T → Sticky Bit without Execute

